                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui ressemble à un pétale ou à une corolle."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d2914aaf-e72d-466d-95e3-00b9d4d6a280",
                                "sense_id": "ee517e2a-765f-3ccd-817f-85a8b5831af3",
                                "text": "M. Dickson dit avoir vu toutes les fleurs d’un Iris pseudacorus ayant un tépale converti en étamine à sommet pétaloïde."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e88d0f98-b6a5-4024-82f4-4c7ccecebf80",
                        "source_entry_id": "fb83138e-b609-3dd4-bde3-17bf487a7a89",
                        "source_sense_id": "ee517e2a-765f-3ccd-817f-85a8b5831af3",
                        "target_lang_word": "petaloid",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "petaloid",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b5150d3-d6bf-3473-b920-064deea82b89",
                                        "entry_id": "d2fce127-fb02-3156-9c44-dc8b6b31bc58",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Resembling the petal of a flower."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00f2a82b-fc5d-4a91-a7e1-dd1c096b6535",
                                                "sense_id": "4b5150d3-d6bf-3473-b920-064deea82b89",
                                                "text": "From whence he concludes, that no apetalous can be a perfect Flower, since the only Fence of a Flower consists in its being petaloid."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08698eb5-7b38-41f0-912c-8d4f6fc0bbca",
                                                "sense_id": "4b5150d3-d6bf-3473-b920-064deea82b89",
                                                "text": "A peach tree, flowering in July for the second time in Kew Gardens, had double flowers, all of which were proliferated, and many of the outermost carpels were petaloid in part."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3e26b4c7-8b84-4de0-a221-58c210ee5c0e",
                                                "sense_id": "4b5150d3-d6bf-3473-b920-064deea82b89",
                                                "text": "On a single bush of Warai-gishi one usually can find some few normal single flowers, flowers with flaglike appendages to the otherwise normal anthers, petaloid filaments with traces of anther left, and completely transformed stamens."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "petaloid",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9c06b891-93bc-3181-b5bf-7d82bf8e9a04",
                                        "entry_id": "a248227b-89b6-31fd-9719-7f6f066410a7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A petaloid structure in a flower."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7219c5c6-752c-4e76-964a-d36ace878a77",
                                                "sense_id": "9c06b891-93bc-3181-b5bf-7d82bf8e9a04",
                                                "text": "Comparative transcriptomic studies among petal, stamen petaloid and stamen through RNA-seq were conducted, which identified several candidate genes involved in stamen petaloid, especially some MADS-box genes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b13384f1-bab6-407e-b260-d2558a0703d2",
                                                "sense_id": "9c06b891-93bc-3181-b5bf-7d82bf8e9a04",
                                                "text": "One or more rows of large outer petals lying flat or undulating, with a mass of intermingled petaloids and stamens in the center."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
